      "description": "Findings about the WHO digital-health corpus in `library/` that are recorded for the owner rather than adopted: where sources disagree, each version kept as an alternative with its citation. `dth-term-alternatives.json` is authored (the one DIIG phase figure and its reproductions, approaches recorded as alternatives, and what \"actor\" means in the RA, SMART Guidelines and folio-assistant, with one proposal per layer); `dth-terms.md` is GENERATED from it and the DTH candidate list by `smart-base:dth-terms` (`smart-base/scripts/gen-dth-term-findings.ts`), and `smart-base:dth-terms:check` fails on a stale page or on a quote that no longer matches its source. A SEPARATE directory from `docs/` because `docs/` is wholly generated by `smart-base:pages`, whose check reports any other file there as an orphan. Owner, 2026-10-03 (#1984, bean `5blc`): \"make a docs page under smart-base showing the glossary/terms differences findings\". `wireframes/` holds the as-is wireframes of the visualisers this instance declares, with what their review found (`check:wireframes` reads the `wireframes/` of every declared `docs` directory): moved here from the platform's docs on 2026-10-20 (wrong-direction move M3), for the same reason the findings are here and not in `docs/`.",
